"suggestion":"Prioritize a unified component system. 1) Standardize shadows: adopt the soft, diffuse shadow style for all interactive elements, including the 'Start Adventure' button, to create a cohesive material feel. 2) Unify button styles: create a single 'secondary button' style (e.g., white pill with dark border) and apply it to both 'How to Play' instances. 3) Finish the 'World Progress' bar: add a colored fill (e.g., 0% width for now, but with a visible track color) to make it look like a functional UI element. 4) Clean up the 'Controls' section: remove the heavy yellow background blocks and use a consistent, subtle background or just clean spacing for all control rows to improve readability and reduce visual noise. 5) Redesign the logo: replace the generic square with a simple, flat bee icon that matches the game's theme. 6) Refine the title typography: consider a flatter, more integrated style for 'Bumble Pop!' that aligns better with the overall clean UI aesthetic, or ensure the 3D effect is consistent with a specific 'game world' style if that is the intent."
